.Dd $Mdocdate: November 24 2026 $
.Dt ANSILOVE_CLEAN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ansilove_clean
.Nd Clean up an ansilove context
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In ansilove.h
.Ft int
.Fn ansilove_clean "struct ansilove_ctx *ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn ansilove_clean
function releases the input file mapping and PNG buffer owned by
.Fa ctx .
The context must have been initialized with
.Xr ansilove_init 3 .
Call this function after conversion, including when loading, rendering,
or saving fails.
.Pp
The
.Va ctx->buffer
pointer is reset to
.Dv MAP_FAILED ,
and
.Va ctx->png.buffer
is reset to
.Dv NULL .
Their associated lengths are reset to zero.
The error code is preserved.
The context structure itself is not freed.
Calling this function again on the same initialized context is safe.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn ansilove_clean
function returns 0, or \-1 if
.Fa ctx
is
.Dv NULL .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ansilove_error 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_init 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_loadfile 3 ,
.Xr ansilove_savefile 3 ,
.Xr libansilove 3
